	(text "PCB BUS CONNECTIONS:\nDescription: Allows the schematic to contain multiple PCBs\nworth of components/netlist info. The power pins\nwith numbers are receiving power. The underscores\nsimply denote which board the pin belongs to,\nin reality ribbon cables will connect these buses together."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 314.198 74.422 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "624a8814-cde7-4fc2-8dd9-4be261c9d7a5")
	)
	(text "<---The control signals are sent out using\n3 bytes (written in serial, output in parallel)\nthrough shift registers.\n\nbyte 0: Analog Sytem\nb0:S0	b4:A0\nb1:S1	b5:A1\nb2:S2	b6:A2\nb3:S3	b7:reserved\n\nbyte 1: LED System\nb0:B0	b4:B4\nb1:B1	b5:B5\nb2:B2	b6:AmplifierEnable\nb3:B3	b7:HallSensorEnable\n\nbyte 2: Motion System\nb0: CoilA	b4: MotorEnable\nb1: CoilB	b5: Gain0\nb2: CoilC	b6: Gain1\nb3: CoilD	b7: Gain2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258.826 136.906 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7929702b-0493-4dca-bdc0-daf78c070a28")
	)
	(text "POWER CONDITIONING:\nDescription: Takes in +5V and GND. GND is common to all components.\n(bar those that don't have ground paths).\n\nACS724xLCTR-10AU - Hall-effect current sensor\n	Power hungry (~14mA quiescent) so has power switch on +5V input\n	Gives us our current reading when we want it, can be enabled with\n	3.3V through the npn->PMOS net.\n\nMCP1700-3302E/TO - 3.3V LDO Voltage Regulator\n	Provides logical 3.3V for chips, bypasses ESP32 3.3V outputs.\n	VSS MUST BE COMMON TO ESP GROUND\n	"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.74 195.072 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "802d4dff-2dea-4132-aa57-e85d28824685")
	)
	(text "REGISTERS:\nDescription: Breaks 3 esp32 output pins into 24.\n74HC595 - CMOS SIPO shift registers"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.352 37.846 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9ec4733b-b08c-4bb6-97be-d13a1a26b7f6")
	)
	(text "MCU"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.102 64.008 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a534c83b-c72d-4e7c-ae2f-7ff21ea4368b")
	)
	(text "PCB BUS CONNNECTIONS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 331.47 63.754 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b963a85a-1a1b-49e8-a459-fc6745d0d6eb")
	)
	(text "Shift Register 0:\n	0 - Analog Mux Channel Select bit0\n	1 - Analog Mux Channel Select bit1\n	2 - Analog Mux Channel Select bit2\n	3 - Analog Mux Channel Select bit3\n	4 - Analog Mux Chip Select bit0\n	5 - Analog Mux Chip Select bit0\n	6 - Analog Mux Chip Select bit0\n	7 - Analog Gain Offset Select\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.036 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "be45a5d1-1319-46c8-b020-d4693c053826")
	)
	(text "<---All signal inputs \nare through this analog channel..."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 259.08 109.728 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dc620919-d5ff-4713-8fe9-68b3ee7a044f")
	)
	(text "ANALOG GAIN:\nDescription: Takes in the common analog signal from\nthe 64-channel analog MUX, passes it through a \nnon-inverting amplifier with programable gain (6-bit)\nand offset (1-bit).\n\nCD4016BCN - CMOS 4-channel analog switch, on-resistance\n~= 200 ohms @ 3.3V supply\nTLV9062SIDGSR - CMOS dual-opamp, low power with shutdown.\nPower hungry, utilize shutdown when ESP enters sleep mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 324.612 193.548 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fdff1b6e-4925-4656-87c8-e893e697158f")
	)
	(text "ANALOG GAIN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.706 177.546 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ff53f5d8-6034-4909-a1a9-9e6def9ce8d9")
	)
